  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Laal maas takes its name from "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "laal ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "laal"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", the Hindi word for red. The colour comes from dried red chillies, ideally the mild "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "mathania chilli ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "mathania-chilli"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". The final stage uses a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "dum",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "dum"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " technique to finish the lamb in sealed steam. Kashmiri chilli powder approximates the colour of mathania chillies if they are unavailable."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Brown the lamb in batches and do not rush the onion stage. Both steps are where the flavour base is built."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
